  "notes": [
    "The metadata read is served at GET /v1/support-grants/{grantId}/metadata (Q1) and fans out to two new internal endpoints owned by Account and Portfolio (BR3.9).",
    "AC3.4.1's screen half belongs to U9 and U10; this unit delivers the API half and changes no frontend file.",
    "NFR2.1–NFR2.5 are implemented by construction (one transaction, no external hop, one conditional UPDATE) and are covered by behaviour tests; their p95/p99 budgets are not measured by a latency test in this unit.",
    "NFR17.3 ships support_read_duration_seconds as designed plus support_write_duration_seconds; the write histogram measures the use case inside the handler, not the full HTTP request, because the repository has no HTTP latency histogram.",
    "support_write_duration_seconds and the four support.grants route labels are additions beyond the plan's enumerated series; both exist so the tenth alert and the write-route dashboard row rest on a real series.",
    "Loop-back 1 (Build and Test, 2026-11-12) adds the F6 line-coverage evidence only: services/portfolio/tests/routes_contract.rs drives every portfolio route the support seam reaches (BR3.9, AC3.4.2), services/account/http/tests/http.rs gains the account listener cases, and services/gateway/tests/adapters.rs and services/gateway/tests/composition.rs exercise the gateway's JWKS, readiness, clock, audit, configuration and composition wiring. These files add test evidence for requirements this table already traces; no requirement or acceptance criterion was added, removed, or retargeted."
